contract.engine_flip_meaning:
[
  "routing_source='engine' means: the navigation-engine (lib/core/navigation-engine.cjs::decide()) has populated decision.fire_skill with a non-null canonical verb. This verb will be fired at the intent-classifier.cjs / skill-activation-router.cjs routeActivation() boundary (lines ~224-246, Precedence Rule 1). The verb was selected by resolveFireSkill() using the wicked_escalation check FIRST, then sensor candidate reaches SECOND, then BRAIN.md pattern_matches verb THIRD. The behavioral meaning: Larry is routing to a SHIPPED capability (one of the 10 canonical verbs or the closed skill families that map from REACH_IDS). The decision came from LOCAL intelligence (sensors fire on local graph + conversational state) + optional BRAIN.md methodology guidance + optional wicked_escalation heuristic for high-wickedness ventures (8+). This is the flip from legacy (routing_source='legacy' = skills/larry-personality default reach set or /command freestyle) to engine (routing_source='engine' = decide() has inferred the next move from the navigation spine, the sensors, and the room's own learning history). In turn-by-turn execution, every time a user commits a reach via closeReach(), the decision writes a typed edge to the room's graph. The next turn, decide() reads that history in the neighborhood (CASC-02 trace.navigated_neighborhood) and uses it as context for the next sensor fires and BRAIN.md queries. This closes the loop: decision -> edge -> neighborhood -> next decide() call. Once the flip is live, the plugin's core mode of operation is guided by the room's own structure, not by Larry's hardcoded reach suggestions."
]
